index 0c22eae..82345b6 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,4 +1,47 @@
 # todo
 
-A small CLI todo manager backed by a JSON file. `python -m todo.cli --file t.json add "x"`.
+A small CLI todo manager. Tasks are stored in **SQLite by default** (`~/.todo.db`,
+standard library `sqlite3` only); the original JSON file backend is still available.
+
+```bash
+todo add "buy milk" --tag home      # writes ~/.todo.db
+todo list --all
+todo done 1
+todo rename 1 "buy oat milk"
+todo rm 1
+```
+
+## Choosing a backend
+
+The backend is picked from the storage path extension via `todo.storage.open_store`:
+
+* `--file tasks.json` → `JsonStore` (whole list rewritten on each change)
+* anything else, e.g. `--file tasks.db` → `SqliteStore` (table `tasks`, full-content
+  replace inside a single transaction)
+
+The path defaults to `~/.todo.db` and can be overridden with `--file PATH` or the
+`TODO_FILE` environment variable.
+
+```bash
+python -m todo.cli --file t.json add "x"   # still JSON
+TODO_FILE=/tmp/todos.db todo list          # still SQLite
+```
+
+## Migrating between backends
+
+`migrate` copies every task from one store to the other — either direction, chosen by
+the file extension — preserving ids, done flags, `created_at` and tags:
+
+```bash
+todo migrate ~/.todo.json ~/.todo.db       # JSON -> SQLite
+todo migrate ~/.todo.db backup.json        # SQLite -> JSON
+# migrated 12 tasks
+```
+
+The destination must be empty; otherwise the command exits `1` with
+`destination not empty` on stderr and leaves the destination untouched. The source is
+never modified, so you can keep both files around.
+
+## Development
+
 Tests: `python -m pytest -q`.
